"cd326570-5cfb-509b-b032-75403ccbfffb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080989 #edb/ref 1080 "y = 2 \\mid x \\mid" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080989 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080989 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fd797849-ceed-5a3a-82c0-cb3e5398f9ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080990 #edb/ref 1080 "y = \\mid x + 2 \\mid" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080990 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080990 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ff53adeb-1f30-5328-a3bf-ff4d5d51695b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080991 #edb/ref 1080 "y = \\mid x \\mid + 2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080991 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080991 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "350503ec-5a13-512f-8efe-e9ff5fd383c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080992 #edb/ref 1080 "y = \\mid x \\mid - 2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080992 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186080992 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6212a032-8185-5ceb-8a00-9014749929a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082947 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14919" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082947 #edb/ref 1071 "Sketch the graph of $y= \\mid x \\mid -3$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082947 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5a2db9be-6ef3-5466-a7cc-4e7e2b5670ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082947 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid +a\n$$\n\nis a vertical translation of the absolute value graph\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\nby $a$ units up.\n\nThe function\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid -3\n$$\n\nhas $a=-3$. Therefore, it is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\nby $3$ units *down*.\n\n![](images/72/7266634257d662b0af75fdb80d402acaa779df2ed4b62fc43c074a7f4f902de0.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082948 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14925" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082948 #edb/ref 1071 "Sketch the graph of $y= \\mid x-3 \\mid$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082948 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2e688f8d-16cc-58d6-8791-538cc335ce04" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082948 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x-a \\mid\n$$\n\nis a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\nby $a$ units right.\n\nThe function\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x-3 \\mid\n$$\n\nhas $a=3$. Therefore, it is a horizontal translation of the absolute value graph\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\nby $3$ units right.\n\n![](images/eb/ebe57ac4935c6ffc84abf20de2959c0f6f543514821ff32900fba65515b55646.png)\n\n**Watch Out!** It's easy to confuse the translations\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x-3 \\mid\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x+3 \\mid\n$$\n\n. The graph of\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x-3 \\mid\n$$\n\nis shifted to the right and the graph of\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x+3 \\mid\n$$\n\nis shifted to the left, even though it seems like it should be the other way around." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082949 #edb/ref 1069 "e-14933" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082949 #edb/ref 1071 "Sketch the graph of $y= \\mid x+1 \\mid +2$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082949 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "82de263c-391b-5d45-bbd6-353c31c806fc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082949 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x-h \\mid +k\n$$\n\nis a translation of the absolute value graph\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\nby $h$ units right and $k$ units up.\n\nThe function\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x+1 \\mid +2\n$$\n\nhas $h=-1$ and $k=2$. Therefore, it is a translation of the absolute value graph\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\nby $1$ unit *left* and $2$ units up.\n\n![](images/e8/e80f640da0a2e6e6c1e14790f66b6a05747f6149dddc8a14fc48932bd5e696eb.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083189 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049534 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083189 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049844 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083189 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083554 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083189 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083189 #edb/ref 1039 "Graphing a Vertical Translation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083189 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186082947 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083189 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "61ec00a6-06ae-5d78-bb1a-b06351432cc3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083190 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083190 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083676 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083190 #edb/ref 1039 "Graphing a Horizontal Translation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083190 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186082948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083190 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "05cffafa-cfcf-5979-a413-b7d0b66dd434" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083191 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083546 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083191 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083191 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186083628 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083191 #edb/ref 1039 "Combining Horizontal and Vertical Translations" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083191 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186082949 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083191 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "ca5dcf12-db1a-5cfc-b369-986caa8f666c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084063 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186084065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1045 "Absolute Value Graphs" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186084061 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049474 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083468 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "da88a97d-6c4e-5299-b921-71200664bd9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083554 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186080219 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083554 #edb/ref 1069 "q-15819" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083554 #edb/ref 1071 "If $y = \\mid x \\mid + 2$, what are the coordinates of the minimum point on the graph?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083554 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "28a546d4-15ea-50f3-baba-d0f944994712" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083676 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186080987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083676 #edb/ref 1069 "q-3677" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083676 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/6e/6e662d75baca8ed3220915e3ff47daf32c4d25c34933a0188e29c404664273c7.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the curve shown above?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083676 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "4d93ade0-ed53-54e6-9369-4b83f3ad2124" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084061 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084062 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084061 #edb/ref 1061 169443 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084061 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "bdb8f706-56c3-508a-a745-c4cf4b268e01" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084061 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084526 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084062 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084063 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084062 #edb/ref 1061 169444 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084062 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6d0878f5-845c-5163-b1ae-e72f37806b6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084062 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084063 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084063 #edb/ref 1061 169447 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084063 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "dfd03723-b5ce-5ca8-98bb-2b1cf56700d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084063 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084064 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186084065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084064 #edb/ref 1061 169450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084064 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3287422a-9367-5f91-9957-0152a7e772df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084064 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186084528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084065 #edb/ref 1061 169451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084065 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "09be9587-52a8-510c-841a-fe31ae2eb30e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084065 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186083191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084526 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's plot the graph of\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\n. According to the algebraic definition of absolute value, we have\n\n$$\n{x\\begin{vmatrix}forx \\ge 0 \\\\ -x\\end{vmatrix}forx < 0\n$$\n\nSo, the left-hand branch of the graph is the function $y=-x$, and the right-hand branch is $y=x$:\n\n![](images/60/60ad4dfdb6086f20f5137c5b4ac4905e55d5697ec4cf31575bf79be5fd408e0c.png)\n\nNotice that the graph has a sharp corner at $(0,0)$. We call this point the **vertex** or the **minimum point.**\n\nWe can apply **horizontal** and **vertical translations** to the graph of\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\n.\n\n- The graph of $y= \\mid x \\mid +a$ is a **vertical translation** of the absolute value graph $y= \\mid x \\mid$. It moves the graph $a$ units up.![](images/bc/bc56f0d75b8359f71a104580902a18a1d8009091b94694beb7f8ac71c9bfc9bc.png)\n- The graph of $y= \\mid x-a \\mid$ is a **horizontal translation** of the absolute value graph $y= \\mid x \\mid$. It moves the graph $a$ units to the *right*.![](images/1f/1f79063f7350e734811366545507fc44c321882d2d9b228b85475a27d46c1759.png)\n\nNote the following:\n\n- When drawing horizontal and vertical translations, it is easiest to transform the graph's vertex first. Then, the two branches can be drawn coming out of the vertex.\n- When we translate the graph $y= \\mid x \\mid$, the resulting curve is called the **image** of $y = \\mid x \\mid$ under the translation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084526 #edb/ref 1065 9295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084526 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "1b8dce6a-8742-581b-80f6-e39c9943b395" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084526 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084528 #edb/ref 1064 "Horizontal and vertical translations can be combined. It does not matter which we do first.\n\nIn general, the graph of\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x-h \\mid +k\n$$\n\nis a translation of the graph\n\n$$\ny= \\mid x \\mid\n$$\n\nby\n\n- $h$ units right, and\n- $k$ units up." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084528 #edb/ref 1065 9302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084528 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b55739df-8b0d-5ef2-9702-d56de0246597" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186084528 #edb/ref 1067 "Combining Translations" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
